#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-sequence-protocol.md:1
msgid "vtkCollection now supports Python sequence protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-sequence-protocol.md:3
msgid ""
"All `vtkCollection` subclasses now support `len()`, indexing with `[]` "
"(including negative indices), and membership testing with `in`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-sequence-protocol.md:6
msgid ""
"collection = vtkActorCollection()\n"
"collection.AddItem(actor1)\n"
"collection.AddItem(actor2)\n"
"\n"
"len(collection)        # 2\n"
"collection[0]          # actor1\n"
"collection[-1]         # actor2\n"
"actor1 in collection   # True\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-sequence-protocol.md:17
msgid ""
"This is implemented at the C level via `tp_as_sequence`, so it is "
"automatically inherited by all ~23 subclasses of `vtkCollection` (e.g., "
"`vtkRendererCollection`, `vtkDataArrayCollection`, etc.) without any "
"additional Python code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-sequence-protocol.md:22
msgid "Pythonic mutation methods are also available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-sequence-protocol.md:24
msgid ""
"collection.append(actor3)     # AddItem\n"
"collection.insert(0, actor4)  # InsertItem\n"
"collection.remove(actor1)     # RemoveItem\n"
"collection.clear()            # RemoveAllItems\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-sequence-protocol.md:31
msgid ""
"All of this is implemented at the C level and automatically inherited by all "
"~23 subclasses of `vtkCollection` (e.g., `vtkRendererCollection`, "
"`vtkDataArrayCollection`, etc.) without any additional Python code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-sequence-protocol.md:35
msgid ""
"The existing iteration protocol (`for item in collection`) continues to work "
"as before."
msgstr ""
